# Python Backend Rule

- Follow existing route/service/model boundaries already present in the backend.
- Keep request handlers thin; push reusable logic into services/helpers.
- Validate inputs and return explicit, stable response shapes.
- Handle external API and database failures with clear errors and logging.
- Update related auth/permission checks when adding sensitive endpoints.

## Safety checks before finishing

- Run or describe API-level verification for touched endpoints.
- Avoid silent exception handling; surface actionable failure details.
